QueenCard is a fork of cc-connect.

Upstream project:
  https://github.com/chenhg5/cc-connect
  Author: chenhg5
  License: MIT (declared in the upstream README and npm/package.json;
  the v1.5.0 snapshot did not ship a LICENSE file)

Baseline: cc-connect v1.5.0, commit 17c61062.

QueenCard is an independent community fork. It is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the cc-connect project. This repository is pinned to the
baseline above and does not follow upstream auto-update. New QueenCard
releases rebase onto a chosen upstream tag on purpose; they are never
installed by running `cc-connect update`.

Thanks to chenhg5 and the cc-connect contributors for the bridge
architecture, agent integrations, and platform support.

QueenCard changes are Copyright (c) 2026 JKL Thinking / jklthinking
and are also released under the MIT License. See LICENSE.

QueenCard v1.5.0-queencard.2 includes:

- Per-bot identity colors, localized four-state Feishu cards, inline
  model/effort selectors, confirmed stop controls, and optional quota hooks.
- Thinking kept out of the reply body for ACP agents (including
  agent_thought_chunk).
- Three-line rich-card status footer (model · effort · elapsed / context
  bar / working directory).
- Codex model-cache priority and six reasoning-effort levels.
- Grok ACP model discovery and effort switching.
- Disabled CLI and in-chat self-update; rebuild from source.
- A source build script for the pinned Linux amd64 binary.
